keywords:
  - "integrative taxonomy"
  - "species delimitation"
  - "Packera"
  - "Asteraceae"
  - "geometric morphometrics"
  - "Elliptic Fourier Analysis"
  - "Euler Characteristic Transform"
  - "herbarium computer vision"
  - "LeafMachine3"
  - "spatial random forest"
abstract: >-
  A six-stage Python and R computational pipeline developed at the University of
  North Carolina at Chapel Hill Herbarium (NCU) for automated vegetative
  phenotyping, nomenclatural type anchoring, determiner authority
  stratification, fine-grain 0 to 15 cm rhizosphere niche modeling, circular
  Hopkins flowering phenology, and five-stage integrative species delimitation
  across North American Packera (Asteraceae: Senecioneae).
